#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""PCGA native PC-store provider foundation (v0.19.6).

This module is deliberately UI-agnostic.  It defines one normalized provider
contract for Epic/Legendary, GOG/gogdl and Amazon/Nile and executes the bundled
Heroic helper binaries directly in a headless container.  v0.19.6 keeps native account connection/disconnection flows for Epic, GOG and Amazon while the owned-game catalog remains read-only. Direct provider game mutation stays blocked; v0.19.6 permits Epic and GOG install jobs only through the separate persistent worker.

Security invariants:
* runner commands are argv arrays; user values are never interpolated into a shell;
* provider credentials stay inside provider-owned config directories;
* diagnostics never return token/auth-file contents;
* catalog refresh may update provider-owned metadata/token caches but never
  changes account ownership or installed games;
* direct provider mutation is limited to explicit login/logout; install plans can only run via the Epic-only job worker (update/verify/uninstall blocked);
* pending device-flow secrets stay server-side and are never returned by diagnostics or the portal.
"""
